      "writtenOn": "2024-11-22T18:26:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have added the following couples of tests to check both cases, not sure how the `ConfigSuite` would suite:\n\n```\npublic void getByEmailIdCaseInsensitive() throws Exception\npublic void getByEmailIdCaseSensitive() throws Exception\n\npublic void lookUpByEmailCaseInsensitive() throws Exception\npublic void lookUpByEmailCaseSensitive() throws Exception\n\npublic void getByNameAndEmailIdCaseInsensitive() throws Exception\npublic void getByNameAndEmailIdCaseSensitive() throws Exception\n```\n\nDid you mean something like this?\n\n```\n@ConfigSuite.Configs\n  public static Map\u003cString, Config\u003e configs() {\n    Config cfgA \u003d new Config();\n    cfgA.setStringList(\"accounts\", null, \"caseInsensitiveLocalPart\", ImmutableList.of(\"example.com\", \"anotherEmailDomain.com\"));\n\n    // All the tests that needed to be tested with \"caseInsensitiveLocalPart\"\n    return ImmutableMap.of(\"getByNameAndEmailId\", cfgA);\n  }\n\n```",
      "parentUuid": "285a472f_a671dd54",
      "revId": "ee5dcd822871f776878352ef2c891cc4750a58d5",
